\section{Regime I: Super-Horizon Cosmology}

We evolve the FRW metric
\[
ds^2 = -c^2 dt^2 + a^2(t)\left(\frac{dr^2}{1-kr^2} + r^2 d\Omega^2\right)
\]
over the domain $r \in [14.3, 1000]$ Gpc.

Key results:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Super-horizon curvature perturbation conserved: $d\zeta_k/dt = 0$
    \item Domain wall surface energy: $\sigma_{\text{wall}} = 8.41\times10^{12}$ GeV$^3$
    \item ADM energy residual: $1.13\times10^{-34}$ J (PASS)
\end{itemize}

